      "id": "n1",
      "kind": "grammar",
      "title": "The small word comes after",
      "text": "Hindi puts the little word after the place: घर में is \"house in\" — \"at home\". The same is true of the other small words you will meet, such as को and पर.",
      "explains": [
        "hi.mein-place"
      ],
      "afterScenes": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "n2",
      "kind": "grammar",
      "title": "है, हैं, हूँ",
      "text": "है goes with one person or thing (रवि है). हैं goes with more than one, and also with people you respect — पापा हैं, आप हैं. हूँ goes only with मैं.",
      "explains": [
        "hi.hai-hain",
        "hi.hum-aap-main"
      ],
      "afterScenes": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "n3",
      "kind": "usage",
      "title": "Yes-no questions",
      "text": "A question without a question word is the same words said with a rising voice: पापा घर में हैं? Answer हाँ or नहीं.",
      "explains": [
        "hi.yes-no-question"
      ],
      "afterScenes": 1
    }
